Art Gallery Management Database System

An advanced database-driven web application designed to manage artists and artworks in an art gallery. This project demonstrates ER modeling, relational database design, constraints, views, and full CRUD operations using Flask and MySQL.

📌 Project Overview

The Art Gallery Management System allows users to:

Manage artist records (name, birthplace, age, style)

Manage artwork records (title, year, category, price)

Maintain relationships between artists and their artworks

Generate reports using SQL Views

Perform full CRUD operations

Enforce database constraints and foreign keys

This project focuses on strong database design principles and practical implementation.

🏗️ Database Design
Entities:

Artists

Artworks

Relationship:

One Artist → Many Artworks (One-to-Many)

Key Features:

Primary Keys & Foreign Keys

CHECK Constraints

ON DELETE CASCADE

SQL Views for reporting

Join Queries

